<title>BELGIUM: EU talks on beef labelling put back.</title>
<headline>EU talks on beef labelling put back.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Talks on two separate proposals for a cattle identification scheme and beef labelling have been put back until after the next European Union farm ministers meeting on Monday, an EU diplomat said.</p>
<p>No agreement could be reached at Tuesday's special committee on agriculture by diplomats preparing the ministers' agenda, the diplomat added.</p>
<p>&quot;There was no agreement and the talks have been put back to another meeting in two weeks time,&quot; the diplomat said.</p>
<p>Ministers will not discuss the two European Commission proposals but will hear a brief progress report from the Dutch presidency of the EU.</p>
</text>
